{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Count trips per filter value"},"description":"Get facet counts for filterable fields, respecting current filters.\n\nCRITICAL: You MUST include ALL established filters in every call \u2014 especially niche, market, adults, children, and arrivalWeeks/arrivalMonths. The facetFields parameter only controls which breakdowns are returned, NOT which filters are applied. If you omit a filter like arrivalWeeks, the counts will include ALL dates \u2014 giving misleading numbers that won't match actual availability for the user's requested dates.\n\nExample \u2014 WRONG: User wants ski in France next week for 2 people. You call get_facets with niche=\"ski\", market=\"dk\", countries=[\"france\"], facetFields=[\"destinationSlug\"]. This returns counts across ALL dates \u2014 showing destinations that may have 0 results for next week.\n\nExample \u2014 RIGHT: Same scenario. You call get_facets with niche=\"ski\", market=\"dk\", countries=[\"france\"], arrivalWeeks=[\"2026-W15\"], adults=2, children=0, facetFields=[\"destinationSlug\"]. This returns only destinations with actual availability for next week with 2 adults.\n\nReturns: { totalCount, facets: { fieldName: { value: count, ... }, ... }, hierarchical }\nhierarchical lists field pairs (e.g. country \u2194 destination) whose bucket counts are not expected to sum to totalCount.\n\nCommon use cases:\n- Check destination availability: facetFields=[\"countrySlug\", \"destinationSlug\"] \u2014 include arrivalWeeks + adults + children\n- Check date availability: facetFields=[\"arrivalYearWeek\", \"arrivalYearMonth\"] \u2014 include destination/country + adults + children\n- Explore filter options: facetFields=[\"durationDays\", \"provider\"] \u2014 include ALL current filters\n- Answer \"where else can I go?\": facetFields=[\"countrySlug\", \"destinationSlug\"] \u2014 include ALL current filters (dates, travelers)\n\n